ed units trade on-exchange while unlisted units deal with the administrator at NAV.\n- **Settlement:** settlement cycles and clearing routes for each class.\n- **Costs:** management fees, ongoing charges, and any entry or exit charges.\n- **Minimums:** minimum initial and holding amounts.\n- **Rights:** voting, income, and redemption rights, and any differences between classes.\n- **Liquidity:** market-maker and authorised-participant arrangements for listed units, versus direct subscription and redemption for unlisted units.\n- **Price:** how exchange prices may diverge from NAV, including premiums and discounts.\n\nI haven't applied any US exemptive-order conditions, as you asked.","ttft_ms":2422,"type":"result","duration_ms":3982,"uuid":"baf864d5-5410-43e3-98e8-4d498e51ddeb","ttft_stream_ms":403,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":403,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
